<title>GERMANY: Siemens confirms 1995/96 results.</title>
<headline>Siemens confirms 1995/96 results.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1996-12-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to Sept 30</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit before extraord.    2,500   vs 2,100</p>
<p>    Group extraordinary profit	     500     vs nil</p>
<p>    Group financial profit	     *   950     vs 1,500</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings per share    *   4.48 DM vs 3.97 DM</p>
<p>    Group sales				  94,200  vs 88,800</p>
<p>	Domestic sales			   36,400  vs 37,900</p>
<p>	Foreign sales			    57,800  vs 50,900</p>
<p>    Group incoming orders		    100,800 vs 91,900</p>
<p>	Domestic orders			  38,000  vs 38,000</p>
<p>	Foreign orders			   62,800  vs 53,900</p>
<p>    Cash-Flow				*   7,700   vs 7,300</p>
<p>    Savings from productivity growth *   8,000   vs 7,000</p>
<p>    Restructuring costs		  *   760     vs 2,200</p>
<p>    Group investments		    *   7,900   vs 7,500</p>
<p>    Group workforce			    379,000 vs 373,000</p>
<p>	Domestic workforce		     203,000 vs 211,000</p>
<p>	Non-domestic			     176,000 vs 162,000</p>
<p>    Dividend				     1.5 DM  vs 1.3 DM</p>
<p>NOTE - Siemens AG announced its profit and other</p>
<p>key financial data in preliminary form on November 6. There were</p>
<p>no significant changes in the final data released today. New</p>
<p>figures are marked (*).</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
